&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About ICE Services&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW259231222 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW259231222 BCX0&quot;&gt;ICE Services&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW259231222 BCX0&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a music technology company built by rightsholders, for rightsholders. We simplify the complexities of the music royalty chain through an innovative suite of licensing, processing, and copyright services, enabling our customers to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW259231222 BCX0&quot;&gt;accurately and efficiently compensate&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW259231222 BCX0&quot;&gt;songwriters and composers&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW259231222 BCX0&quot;&gt;for the use of their works.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW259231222 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;A joint venture between PRS, STIM, and GEMA, ICE Services is the result of a big vision for the industry that harnesses years of combined experience in the multi-territory music market.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Serving over 330,000 rightsholders and leveraging a copyright database comprising 55 million musical works, ICE Services’ operations touch 250+ territories to distribute more than €1bn in royalties per year, with a total of over €5bn distributed to date.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;We’re based in the UK, Germany, and Sweden.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;page&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;layoutArea&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;column&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Backend Engineer, you will play a pivotal role in the development and enhancement of our new copyright product. Your responsibilities will include hands-on product engineering, working with a team of talented product engineers, designing and implementing complex systems, and collaborating with cross-functional teams to deliver exceptional products to our customers. If you thrive in a collaborative environment and possess a keen eye for detail, this is an excellent opportunity to contribute to groundbreaking projects and shape the future of the ICE Services&#39; product portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re building a strong foundation for our company on these products. Bringing the technical expertise in-house and being part of a modern, product-centric technology organisation that works based on agile methodologies and principles are key pillars of our technology strategy. We’re creating the kind of teams talked about in Inspired by Marty Cagan, and following principles in Accelerate by Nicole Forsgren.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;page&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;layoutArea&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;column&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Technology Stack&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our copyright product is primarily running in AWS with the following technologies:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Java SpringBoot Microservices • DynamoDB&lt;br&gt;• OpenSearch&lt;br&gt;• Postgres&lt;br&gt;• S3&lt;br&gt;• Kinesis&lt;br&gt;• SNS&lt;br&gt;• SQS&lt;br&gt;• Docker / ECS / EKS • Serverless frameworks&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;page&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;layoutArea&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;column&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and Implement: Work as part of a product engineering team to design and implement complex software systems, ensuring scalability, reliability, and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration: Collaborate with product managers and cross-functional teams to define product requirements and create comprehensive technical specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Code Reviews: Conduct thorough code reviews, providing constructive feedback to maintain code quality and adherence to best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Ownership: Take ownership of critical technical decisions and provide expert guidance in selecting appropriate technologies and tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Development Practices: Champion best development practices, includ- ing code documentation, unit testing, and version control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Risk Mitigation: Identify and mitigate technical risks, proactively ad- dressing potential challenges throughout the product development lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry Trends: Stay up-to-date with the latest industry trends and advancements, integrating new technologies to enhance product offerings and maintain a competitive edge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-Assisted Engineering: Embrace AI-powered tools (e.g., coding assistants, automated testing, intelligent search) as productivity multipliers, and explore opportunities where AI can enhance our copyright products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentoring: Mentor and coach junior engineers, fostering a culture of continuous learning and professional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements and Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience: 5 to 7 years of relevant experience in product engineering. Previous experience in a senior or lead engineering role is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Expertise: Demonstrated expertise in programming languages such as Java alongside proficiencies in web technologies, database management, and cloud platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven Track Record: A history of designing, developing, and delivering successful software products from concept to launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration Skills: Ability to work collaboratively with product managers, designers, and other stakeholders to translate product requirements into technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication Skills: Clear and effective communication skills, both written and verbal, to convey technical concepts to technical and non-technical audiences alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovation: A passion for innovation, including openness to leveraging AI-powered tools and technologies in daily engineering work. Commitment to staying abreast of emerging technologies and industry trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality Focus: A strong commitment to code quality, unit testing, and other best practices in software engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptability: The ability to thrive in a fast-paced and rapidly evolving environment, with a willingness to take on new challenges and responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-Solving: Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills to resolve complex technical challenges.
&lt;div class=&quot;page&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;layoutArea&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;column&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;page&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;layoutArea&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What we offer:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive local benefits based on your location&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We promote flexible working regarding time and/or place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Both mental and physical health initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Corporate pension scheme&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive training and development opportunities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry insider events, team socials and company events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced holiday allowance&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome candidates from all backgrounds, regardless of age, disability, gender, gender identity, gender expression, race, religion or belief, sexual orientation, socioeconomic background, and any other protected characteristic.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to making all stages of our recruitment process accessible to candidates with disabilities. Please speak to our recruitment team and we will work with you to make reasonable adjustments to ensure you can perform at your best throughout your application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; London / Hybrid&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duration:&lt;/strong&gt; 6-12 Months&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Day Rate:&lt;/strong&gt; £340 - £360 per day&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engagement Method&lt;/strong&gt;: Umbrella/PAYE&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Digital Designer&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Creative Services team for an initial 6-12 month&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;period. Please note this role has been assessed as Inside IR35, and payment will be processed via PAYE or an umbrella company through our third-party partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an in-house creative organization for Sony PlayStation® that specializes in marketing everything PlayStation® related. The Global Creative Team is seeking a an experienced, hands-on, creative, and detail-focused Senior Digital Experience Designer to join forces with our team &amp;amp; contribute their design experiences and co-lead the delivery for our creative project marketing touchpoints worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will report to the Sr Design Manager to liaise with other cross-functional departments and deliver Digital creative for mid to high complexity projects on schedule and on-brand. Our work is seen by millions, from national retail environments to limited edition hardware, to exclusive game titles, to official PlayStation® apparel that fans wait hours in line to get their hands on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as one of the design leads for key PlayStation.com and CRM projects, while supporting our expanding workload across a wide range of initiatives, including game / hardware launches, brand and sales campaigns, emails, new business initiatives, UI/UX support, and other creative projects. Support the development and enhancement of SIE brand best practices, production techniques, and workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-Lead the day-to-day digital design &amp;amp; production tasks of layout, template-building, edits, and final file prep for PlayStation.com &amp;amp; CRM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define page design and user flows for new &amp;amp; existing pages across the end-to-end journey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take direction from other design leads and support and oversee the work of more junior members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate and communicate with design leadership, project managers, and traffic coordinators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross functional teams to ensure the work and production quality meets PlayStation® brand and design standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present design efforts in front of small groups, over email, and/or through visual presentations to a wide audience of various backgrounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take initiatives to better understand industry and competitor approaches through in-store, online, and design publication research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop Localized artwork for PlayStation.com &amp;amp; CRM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rework game and hardware assets into various banners for PlayStation.com &amp;amp; CRM, to meet the standard requirements for publishing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support updating Marketing brand and technical guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in digital and production design within a dynamic marketing environment, gained either in-house or at an agency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience designing web, mobile and CRM layouts in Figma using established design-system components, with a proven ability to optimize user journeys for clarity, efficiency, and conversion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert knowledge of Figma &amp;amp; Adobe Creative Cloud &amp;amp; (Photoshop, Illustrator, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design theory, including layout, color, typography, hierarchy, as well as current design trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to conceptualize in quick, broad strokes and big, creative ways, but able to see ideas through to the last details of file organization and clean-up, adhering to template specs, proofing content, and spellchecking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing across a wide variety of digital media and formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to follow design instructions and implement style guides.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a challenging, fast-paced, and dynamic corporate environment while staying deadline-focused on multiple projects with composure and ease.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible, team player, devoid of ego, with enthusiasm for collaboration and a willingness to take direction and offer own insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment is a Fair Chance employer and qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records will be considered for employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
